{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>Here, these.</b> This tells that they recognized them — this is the one in whom so-and-so stumbled (Yalkut Shimoni 585)." "<b>Through the matter of Balaam.</b> He said to them: Even if you bring all the multitudes in the world you cannot prevail against them — are you more numerous than the Egyptians, who had six hundred chosen chariots? Come and I will advise you counsel — their Elohim hates licentiousness, etc., as is found in Ḥelek (106a) and in Sifrei."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:13:24.338485169Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}